# A complaint answered (IDEAS I20 b, I25 a; QUESTIONS Q29, 3; board 0.4): it failed until a dragged window floated.
# Story: a person moves windows about as on any Mac. Near a screen edge, near another window: nothing of Arbor's shows and nothing
# docks. Holding ⌘ while dragging asks Arbor. macOS's own tiling is off here, so that the edges would be Arbor's to take.
mac-tiling off
open Safari
open Notes
pick-up 101 2 400
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 101
expect count docked 0
# With ⌘ held it docks there. (From somewhere else: the simulator's hand takes a title bar by its middle, which now lies in the edge's band,
# and a hand that takes hold within the band and never leaves it has carried nothing there, ⌘ or not: a ⌘-click that slips docks nothing.)
drag 101 600 300
expect floating 101
drag 101 2 400 cmd
expect docked 101
# Beside a docked window, plainly: it floats where it was let go.
pick-up 102 650 400
wait 1
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 102
expect still 101
# A docked window dragged plainly comes out, at the size it had before Arbor sized it.
drag 101 700 300
expect floating 101
expect size 101 640x420
expect count docked 0
# ⌘ may go down on the way, and the preview comes with it; it comes up again before the window is let go, and nothing docks.
pick-up 102 2 400
expect preview none
cmd down
expect preview showing
cmd up
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 102
expect count docked 0
# A click on a docked window's title bar that slips by a few points takes nothing out.
dock 101 left
drag 101 366 55
expect docked 101
expect still 102
# One setting brings back the first build's way, another lets no drag dock.
set dragDocks always
drag 102 1438 400
expect docked 102
set dragDocks never
drag 102 700 300
expect floating 102
drag 102 1438 400 cmd
expect floating 102
